## Why This Is Asked
Real-world multi-tenant analytics require dynamic, fair scheduling under CKNE pressure.

## Key Concepts
- Fixed compute pool vs dynamic per-tenant quotas
- CKNE-to-weight mapping and minimum SLA
- Minute-level rebalancing with capped drift
- Preemption vs graceful completion, telemetry

## Code Example
```javascript
function rebalance(tenants, S){
  // tenants: {id, ckne, slots, m_i}
  const sumCKNE = tenants.reduce((a,t)=>a+t.ckne,0);
  tenants.forEach(t=>{ t.target = Math.max(t.m_i, Math.floor(S * (t.ckne / sumCKNE) ));});
  // sort by ckne; move deltas within deltaLimit
}
```

